WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.140
JENNY BROWN: Today we're
talking about Next '21 data loss

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.110
protection and Google
Distributed Cloud.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:10.500
I'm Jenny Brown, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.500
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.650
Google Cloud Next '21 is
over, but the learning

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.030
is just beginning.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.720
With three days of keynotes,
deep dives, and announcements,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.580
there was a lot to take in.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.800
But don't worry if
you missed something.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.570
The Google Cloud
blog team is here

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.820
to round up our
favorite announcements.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.950
Check out the blog for more.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.600
Data is one of your
most valuable assets,

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.240
so we're happy to
announce that we're

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.260
making Cloud DLP automatic--
automatic discovery,

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.520
automatic inspection, automatic
classification, automatic data

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.480
profiling.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.000
Now available in
preview for BigQuery,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.200
you can enable Cloud DLP
across your entire organization

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.920
to gain visibility
into your data risk.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.560
Organizations are looking
to accelerate their cloud

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.470
adoption.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.760
However, some of their workloads
can't move to the public cloud

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.870
entirely or right away, due
to a variety of factors.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.940
To ensure these
workloads can still

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.490
take advantage of what
the cloud has to offer,

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.770
we announced Google
Distributed Cloud,

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:18.050
a portfolio of
solutions consisting

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:21.740
of hardware and software that
extend your infrastructure

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.230
to the edge and into
your data centers.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.170
Check out the full
details on the blog.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.630
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.400
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.010
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.030
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.200
We'll see you in the cloud.

